WEBVTT

00:30.000 --> 00:36.400
Cheonggwan expresses sky, the root of everything in the universe and the universe itself,

00:36.400 --> 00:40.400
and the imagery world that has its being in the sky.

00:40.400 --> 00:46.000
The progress line of Cheonggwan Pumsae that represents the infinite potential of the sky

00:46.000 --> 00:51.600
that expresses creation, change and completion is the Korean vowel Woo.

00:53.600 --> 00:57.600
We will now take a look at the key moves of Cheonggwan Pumsae.

01:00.000 --> 01:02.000
Cheonggwan Pumsae

01:30.000 --> 01:32.000
Woo!

02:00.000 --> 02:02.000
Cheonggwan Pumsae

02:02.000 --> 02:04.000
Cheonggwan Pumsae

02:04.000 --> 02:06.000
Cheonggwan Pumsae

02:28.000 --> 02:32.000
Cheonggwan Pumsae consists of seven key moves,

02:32.000 --> 02:34.000
stabbing the fist of the night,

02:36.000 --> 02:38.000
swallowing the wings,

02:42.000 --> 02:44.000
blocking with the whistle,

02:48.000 --> 02:50.000
pulling with the whistle,

02:52.000 --> 02:54.000
stabbing the side of the golden river,

02:56.000 --> 02:58.000
pushing the mountain,

03:02.000 --> 03:04.000
and

03:08.000 --> 03:14.000
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Cheonggwan Pumsae.

03:14.000 --> 03:24.000
Bamjumeokjijirigi is a technique to thrust and strike a target at chin elevation from the waist up using the knuckle fist.

03:24.000 --> 03:26.000
The elbows should face downward,

03:26.000 --> 03:28.000
and the armpits should touch the ground.

03:28.000 --> 03:30.000
The elbows should face downward,

03:30.000 --> 03:32.000
and the armpits should touch the body.

03:34.000 --> 03:36.000
Be careful not to let the elbow open outward,

03:36.000 --> 03:38.000
creating space under the arm.

03:40.000 --> 03:42.000
Natgebyogi should be performed slowly.

03:46.000 --> 03:48.000
Start with Gyeopsong.

03:48.000 --> 03:50.000
Raise the hand to the front of the chest,

03:50.000 --> 03:52.000
then inhale.

03:54.000 --> 03:56.000
When both hands are in front of the chest,

03:56.000 --> 03:58.000
pull the wrists back.

03:58.000 --> 04:00.000
Push both palms outward and exhale.

04:04.000 --> 04:08.000
Remember that the wrists should not straighten when pushing the hands.

04:12.000 --> 04:16.000
Hridulomaki is a technique to draw a big circle with the arm

04:16.000 --> 04:18.000
and block by swinging the outer wrist.

04:20.000 --> 04:22.000
This is a soft move,

04:22.000 --> 04:24.000
so perform the move without disconnect

04:24.000 --> 04:26.000
and make sure not to pause abruptly.

04:30.000 --> 04:32.000
Hridulojabadangigi

04:32.000 --> 04:34.000
is a technique where you open the hand

04:34.000 --> 04:36.000
and draw a big circle,

04:36.000 --> 04:38.000
block by swinging,

04:38.000 --> 04:40.000
then pull an opponent's arm.

04:40.000 --> 04:42.000
This move must also be performed smoothly

04:42.000 --> 04:44.000
in motion like Hridulomaki.

04:46.000 --> 04:48.000
Start with Jjageundoljogui

04:48.000 --> 04:50.000
to block the face and thrust.

04:50.000 --> 04:54.000
Thrusting in the Yeopuro Nolpyosugi posture

04:54.000 --> 04:56.000
is called Yeopjjireugi.

04:58.000 --> 05:00.000
Both fists must not start jjireugi from the waist.

05:04.000 --> 05:06.000
Start with both hands from the waist

05:06.000 --> 05:08.000
and perform Tesanmilgi with the palm of your hand.

05:10.000 --> 05:12.000
Push the palm of your hand forward

05:12.000 --> 05:14.000
to lower abdomen elevation on the same side

05:14.000 --> 05:16.000
as the front foot

05:16.000 --> 05:18.000
with the tip of the hand facing downward.

05:18.000 --> 05:20.000
Push the palm hand forward

05:20.000 --> 05:22.000
to philtrum elevation

05:22.000 --> 05:24.000
on the same side as the hind foot

05:24.000 --> 05:26.000
with the tip of the hand facing upward.

05:28.000 --> 05:30.000
Both hands must form a straight line

05:30.000 --> 05:32.000
with the center line

05:32.000 --> 05:34.000
and your arms should straighten naturally.

05:38.000 --> 05:40.000
Be careful not to let your shoulders rise.

05:44.000 --> 05:46.000
For Wendikubi,

05:46.000 --> 05:48.000
Jjireugi is a technique

05:48.000 --> 05:50.000
where you move while your center is placed

05:50.000 --> 05:52.000
on your left leg.

05:52.000 --> 05:54.000
Maintain the Duikubi posture

05:54.000 --> 05:56.000
by pulling your left foot

05:56.000 --> 05:58.000
the moment your right foot pushes

05:58.000 --> 06:00.000
and sets forward about a half step.

06:00.000 --> 06:02.000
Do not set your foot forward

06:02.000 --> 06:04.000
after pulling your hind leg.

06:06.000 --> 06:08.000
These are the 7 key moves

06:08.000 --> 06:10.000
of Cheonggwanpoomsae.

06:12.000 --> 06:14.000
We will now look at the moves in succession

06:14.000 --> 06:16.000
connecting each move.

06:18.000 --> 06:20.000
The key moves of Cheonggwan first part

06:20.000 --> 06:22.000
consist of

06:44.000 --> 06:46.000
Jjireugi,

06:46.000 --> 06:48.000
Wensonna Bitureomakki,

06:48.000 --> 06:50.000
Wenhand Gama Jabaggulmyo,

06:50.000 --> 06:52.000
and Jyeopjagi,

06:52.000 --> 06:54.000
and Wenaremakki,

06:54.000 --> 06:56.000
and Orenjireugi.

06:58.000 --> 07:00.000
When performing Dubamchumok Jjijireugi

07:00.000 --> 07:02.000
followed by Nagepyogi,

07:02.000 --> 07:04.000
lower your arms

07:04.000 --> 07:06.000
and place your hands in front of your lower abdomen.

07:10.000 --> 07:12.000
Draw a circle across your chest

07:12.000 --> 07:14.000
moving above your head

07:14.000 --> 07:16.000
and draw a circle by scattering both hands sideways.

07:18.000 --> 07:20.000
Move the hand to both the waist

07:20.000 --> 07:22.000
with the back of the hand facing upward

07:22.000 --> 07:24.000
and perform Bamchumok Jjijireugi.

07:26.000 --> 07:28.000
When performing Nagepyogi,

07:28.000 --> 07:30.000
scatter an opponent's attempt to grab

07:30.000 --> 07:32.000
or attack with a headbutt

07:32.000 --> 07:34.000
by using both hands.

07:34.000 --> 07:36.000
Then strike an opponent under the chin

07:36.000 --> 07:38.000
or the lower part of the face

07:38.000 --> 07:40.000
with Bamchumok Jjijireugi.

07:40.000 --> 07:42.000
Bitureomakki is a technique

07:42.000 --> 07:44.000
used to block with the hand

07:44.000 --> 07:46.000
opposite the foot set forward

07:46.000 --> 07:48.000
by slightly twisting the body.

07:48.000 --> 07:50.000
In Cheonggwan Pumsae,

07:50.000 --> 07:52.000
pull the hind leg lightly

07:52.000 --> 07:54.000
and block by twisting the torso.

07:54.000 --> 07:56.000
This technique enables a quick

07:56.000 --> 07:58.000
and strong counterattack

07:58.000 --> 08:00.000
since you can attack by unraveling the twisted torso.

08:02.000 --> 08:04.000
When performing Wenhand Gama Jabaggulmyo Jjireugi,

08:04.000 --> 08:06.000
move your center forward

08:06.000 --> 08:08.000
while coiling and grabbing

08:08.000 --> 08:10.000
an opponent's wrist

08:10.000 --> 08:12.000
by twisting your left hand outward.

08:14.000 --> 08:16.000
Then move the body closer to the arm

08:16.000 --> 08:18.000
and pull with a strong force.

08:20.000 --> 08:22.000
Perform slowly,

08:22.000 --> 08:24.000
maximizing the force used.

08:26.000 --> 08:28.000
When performing the opposite

08:28.000 --> 08:30.000
Orunhand Gama Jabaggulmyo Jjireugi,

08:30.000 --> 08:32.000
twist the right hand outward.

08:34.000 --> 08:36.000
When performing Orunseona Bitureomakki,

08:38.000 --> 08:40.000
pull your right foot slightly forward.

08:44.000 --> 08:46.000
Pull your foot and move your center

08:46.000 --> 08:48.000
slightly forward.

08:50.000 --> 08:52.000
When connecting Wenhand Gama Jabaggulmyo Jjireugi,

08:52.000 --> 08:54.000
Yopchagi,

08:56.000 --> 08:58.000
and Wenaremakki,

08:58.000 --> 09:00.000
pull the left arm in the opposite direction

09:00.000 --> 09:02.000
and perform Yopchagi with a shout.

09:02.000 --> 09:04.000
When performing Orun Jjireugi,

09:04.000 --> 09:06.000
set your foot without any change in elevation.

09:10.000 --> 09:12.000
Cautions for Cheonggwan first part,

09:12.000 --> 09:14.000
taking a closer look.

09:16.000 --> 09:18.000
When pushing both hands during Nalgaepbyeoggi,

09:18.000 --> 09:20.000
be careful not to let the wrist straighten.

09:22.000 --> 09:24.000
Dupamjumeok Jjijireugi

09:24.000 --> 09:26.000
must be connected with the right arm

09:26.000 --> 09:28.000
and pull with a strong force.

09:28.000 --> 09:30.000
Dupamjumeok Jjijireugi

09:30.000 --> 09:32.000
must be connected without pause.

09:34.000 --> 09:36.000
When performing Wenseona Bitureomakki,

09:36.000 --> 09:38.000
the foot must not move

09:38.000 --> 09:40.000
outside the body during Apgubi.

09:42.000 --> 09:44.000
When performing Wenhand Gama Jabaggulmyo Jjireugi,

09:46.000 --> 09:48.000
do not lift the left elbow outward.

09:54.000 --> 09:56.000
When performing Bitureomakki,

09:56.000 --> 09:58.000
head elevation must not change.

10:00.000 --> 10:02.000
When performing Orun Hand Gama Jabaggulmyo Jjireugi,

10:04.000 --> 10:06.000
do not lift the right elbow outward.

10:12.000 --> 10:14.000
We will now practice the moves of Cheonggwan first part

10:14.000 --> 10:16.000
in succession while watching the video.

10:26.000 --> 10:28.000
Cheonggwan

10:56.000 --> 11:00.200
The key moves of Cheonggwon's second part consist of

11:00.200 --> 11:03.300
웬 안팔목 꼬도로 바깥 막기

11:03.300 --> 11:05.700
휘두러 막고 찌르기

11:05.700 --> 11:09.500
웬 핸드 초쩌내며 잡아당겨 오른찌르기

11:09.500 --> 11:12.600
오른 안팔목 꼬도로 바깥 막기

11:12.600 --> 11:16.500
오른 핸드 초쩌내며 잡아당겨 왼찌르기

11:16.500 --> 11:21.600
and 오른 핸드 초쩌내며 잡아당겨 오른찌르기

11:21.600 --> 11:25.100
When performing 웬 안팔목 꼬도로 바깥 막기

11:25.100 --> 11:30.800
elevation of your right arm should be the same as your left elbow, but horizontal.

11:30.800 --> 11:37.400
Be careful not to let the tip of your left fist rise over your shoulder.

11:37.400 --> 11:40.600
When swinging, blocking and thrusting the torso,

11:40.600 --> 11:46.400
turn your left arm over inward during 꼬도로 안팔목 바깥 막기

11:46.400 --> 11:50.000
and lower it to the inside of your body.

11:50.000 --> 11:54.600
Then swing above the head and block like 얼굴 막기.

11:54.700 --> 11:59.100
Pull to the back left, then connect to 찌르기.

11:59.100 --> 12:04.500
When connecting your 웬 핸드 초쩌내며 잡아당기기 to 오른찌르기,

12:04.500 --> 12:11.000
open your left hand, draw a big circle to swing and block, then pull an opponent's arm.

12:11.000 --> 12:13.500
This move must be connected smoothly

12:13.500 --> 12:19.100
while moving forward with minimal change in head elevation.

12:19.100 --> 12:25.200
Cautions for 청관 2nd part, taking a closer look.

12:25.200 --> 12:28.200
When performing 휘두로 막고 찌르기,

12:28.200 --> 12:32.100
the moves must not be disconnected or rigid.

12:32.100 --> 12:36.600
Concentrate on connecting them smoothly.

12:36.600 --> 12:42.700
The same goes for the 웬 핸드 초쩌내며 잡아당겨 오른찌르기 move.

12:42.700 --> 12:48.900
Do not disconnect or pause the moves. Connect them smoothly.

12:50.100 --> 12:54.100
We will now practice the moves of 청관 2nd part in succession

12:54.100 --> 12:56.900
while watching the video.

13:12.300 --> 13:15.800
The key moves of 청관 3rd part consist of

13:15.800 --> 13:18.800
오른 안팔목 삐뚤어 막기

13:18.800 --> 13:23.000
웬 찌르기, 오른 앞차기 and 오른 찌르기,

13:23.000 --> 13:25.600
오른 손나 거드로 아래 막기,

13:25.600 --> 13:30.500
and 오른 안팔목 바깥 막기 and 거드로 아래 막기.

13:30.500 --> 13:33.700
When performing 오른 안팔목 삐뚤어 막기,

13:33.700 --> 13:40.100
draw a circle with the right hand inside the torso and block with one motion.

13:40.100 --> 13:45.800
The upper body should twist 45 degrees.

13:45.900 --> 13:49.500
When taking the 1st half step with 자전 발,

13:49.500 --> 13:54.800
during the connection of 오른 안팔목 바깥 막기 and 거드로 아래 막기,

13:54.800 --> 14:01.800
perform 오른 안팔목 몸통 막기.

14:01.800 --> 14:09.000
Strike the forearm moving upward with a forefinger gathered left palm.

14:09.000 --> 14:11.200
When taking the 2nd half step,

14:11.300 --> 14:16.300
lower the right elbow again and perform 아래 막기.

14:16.300 --> 14:22.400
This time, strike the right forearm with the left palm and clench the fist.

14:22.400 --> 14:29.100
These moves must be connected quickly.

14:29.100 --> 14:34.200
Cautions for 청관 3rd part, taking a closer look.

14:34.200 --> 14:37.300
When performing 오른 안팔목 삐뚤어 막기,

14:37.300 --> 14:43.000
beware that your center will weaken if your upper body twists excessively.

14:43.000 --> 14:45.500
The same goes for 왼주리기.

14:45.500 --> 14:51.000
Do not excessively twist the upper body.

14:51.000 --> 14:58.000
When connecting 오른 안팔목 바깥 막기 and 거드로 아래 막기,

14:58.000 --> 15:03.600
pull the hind foot first and do not set the front foot forward.

15:03.600 --> 15:10.300
We will now practice the moves of 청관 3rd part in succession while watching the video.

15:21.300 --> 15:25.100
The key moves of 청관 4th part consist of

15:25.100 --> 15:27.300
오른 끔감 옆 찌르기,

15:27.300 --> 15:30.400
뛰어 360도 돌아 표적차기,

15:30.400 --> 15:33.400
and 끔감 오른 옆 찌르기.

15:33.400 --> 15:47.500
변손 외산들 아래 막기.

15:47.500 --> 15:52.000
대산 밀기

15:52.000 --> 15:57.500
and 대산 밀기.

15:57.500 --> 16:00.200
When performing 끔감 옆 찌르기,

16:00.300 --> 16:03.800
start with 오른 작은 돌적위.

16:03.800 --> 16:07.800
Block your face and perform 찌르기.

16:07.800 --> 16:11.900
When connecting 뛰어 360도 돌아 표적차기

16:11.900 --> 16:15.000
and 끔감 오른 옆 찌르기,

16:15.000 --> 16:18.700
shift your weight on your right foot for airborne 표적차기

16:18.700 --> 16:22.900
and jump in the air by kicking the ground.

16:22.900 --> 16:31.300
Then, twist your body to the left and spin 360 degrees midair.

16:31.300 --> 16:36.100
The left foot will set on the ground while the body is spinning in midair.

16:36.100 --> 16:43.000
Kick the palm of your left hand, the target, with your right foot blade before setting your foot.

16:43.000 --> 16:47.800
Your left foot must not touch the ground before kicking the target.

16:47.800 --> 16:50.500
Start with 오른 작은 돌적위.

16:50.500 --> 16:54.800
Block your face, then connect with 찌르기.

16:54.800 --> 17:00.200
When performing 대산 밀기, turn your body to the left.

17:00.200 --> 17:05.800
Get up by pulling your left foot, then assume the 모아석이 posture.

17:05.800 --> 17:09.300
Place both hands in front of the lower abdomen.

17:09.300 --> 17:14.900
Raise them above the head, then lower them drawing a circle on both sides.

17:14.900 --> 17:17.800
Bend the elbows at torso elevation.

17:17.800 --> 17:22.400
Place them in front of the solar plexus.

17:22.400 --> 17:30.200
Bring the palms of your hands close to your body, right hand facing downward, left hand facing upward.

17:30.200 --> 17:32.600
Set your right foot forward.

17:32.600 --> 17:36.700
Push the palms of your hands below and above forward

17:36.700 --> 17:42.300
by extending your elbows while assuming the 오른 범석이 posture.

17:42.300 --> 17:49.200
Perform the more slowly exerting force in the lower abdomen.

17:49.200 --> 17:53.400
Push the left palm of your hand to philtrum elevation,

17:53.400 --> 17:58.600
the right palm of your hand below to the lower abdomen elevation.

17:58.600 --> 18:03.600
Place both hands again, like 옙손, in front of the lower abdomen.

18:03.600 --> 18:09.300
Raise them above your head, and lower them drawing a circle on both sides.

18:09.300 --> 18:11.900
Bend the elbows at torso elevation.

18:11.900 --> 18:16.900
Place them in front of the solar plexus, then bend back the wrists.

18:16.900 --> 18:20.500
This time, perform the move in the opposite direction.

18:20.500 --> 18:23.300
Bring the palm of your hands close to your body,

18:23.300 --> 18:27.400
with the right hand facing upward and the left hand facing downward.

18:27.400 --> 18:29.100
Set your left foot forward.

18:29.100 --> 18:32.500
Push the palms of your hands below and above forward

18:32.500 --> 18:38.200
by extending your elbows while assuming the 왼 범석이 posture, like the previous move.

18:38.200 --> 18:42.200
Perform the move slowly, exerting force in the lower abdomen.

18:42.200 --> 18:45.800
Push the right palm of your hand above to philtrum elevation,

18:45.800 --> 18:50.600
the left palm of your hand below to lower abdomen elevation.

18:50.600 --> 18:54.800
Cautions for 청관 4th part, taking a closer look.

18:54.800 --> 18:57.600
When performing 오른 금강 옆 지르기,

18:57.600 --> 19:02.300
do not perform 지르기 with both fists next to the waist.

19:02.300 --> 19:06.300
When connecting 뛰어 360도 돌아 표적차기

19:06.300 --> 19:09.200
and 금강 오른 옆 지르기,

19:09.200 --> 19:13.600
the left foot must not touch the ground before kicking the target,

19:13.600 --> 19:18.000
and 지르기 must not start from the waist.

19:18.000 --> 19:21.400
When performing the first 대산 밀기,

19:21.400 --> 19:25.400
set the right foot first.

19:25.400 --> 19:28.000
When performing the second 대산 밀기,

19:28.000 --> 19:34.900
set the left foot first.

19:34.900 --> 19:41.700
We will now practice the moves of 청관 4th part in succession while watching the video.

20:04.900 --> 20:08.700
This concludes the training for 청관 품세.

20:08.700 --> 20:12.700
We will take another look at all the moves and master 품세.

21:34.900 --> 21:54.000
We have looked at the key moves of 청관 품세

21:54.000 --> 21:59.500
and provided thorough explanations for each move and things to watch out for.

21:59.500 --> 22:05.100
Be mindful of the spirit of 청관 that embodies the infinite sky with training,

22:05.100 --> 22:10.000
and you will be able to master the intricate moves accurately.

22:10.000 --> 22:13.900
We will see you again in the Hanzu 품세 video.

22:13.900 --> 22:15.400
Thanks for watching.

